menu "Gateway: storage"

    config GW_CONFIG_MAX_BYTES
        int "Largest accepted /cfg/config.json (bytes)"
        range 4096 1048576
        default 131072
        help
            The spec maximum (16 devices, 256 tags with every field) is about 46 KB of
            compact JSON and 82 KB indented with 2 spaces. The file and the parser's
            document tree (about 200 KB for 256 tags) are allocated at boot, in PSRAM
            when present, and freed before the gateway starts. A larger file is
            rejected: the gateway then stays stopped with the configuration error state.

    choice GW_SF_SPILL
        prompt "Store & forward spill (SPB-14, sparkplug.store_forward.sd)"
        default GW_SF_SPILL_SDMMC
        help
            Where the store & forward ring spills when it is full, if the configuration
            enables it (off by default). GPIO45, the card's D0, is a strapping pin: see
            README 6.5 before enabling it on a board.

        config GW_SF_SPILL_SDMMC
            bool "microSD card on SDMMC, 1-bit (CLK 48, CMD 47, D0 45)"

        config GW_SF_SPILL_LITTLEFS
            bool "A directory of the LittleFS partition (QEMU stand-in for the card)"

        config GW_SF_SPILL_NONE
            bool "None"
    endchoice

endmenu
